  "question": {
    "text": "If the tangent to the curve&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math> at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> and the normal to the parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> intersect at the same point on the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;is ....."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For the parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So, equation of normal is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;intersects <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Given curve&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math></p><p>So, equation of&nbsp;tangent to the curve at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>At&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
